@*
    Tokens.cshtml — the ESC /admin/escalation/tokens receiving-token surface
    (ADR 0159, ESC·3 / ESC·9 / ESC·12).

    The receiving GlobalAdmin's token lifecycle:
      - A **generate** form (the Label input + the
        escalation.tokens.generate.button button, the U07 closed set). A
        [ValidateAntiForgeryToken] POST to …/generate (the
        IEscalationTokenService.GenerateAsync single-write-lane, ESC·3 /
        ESC·9). On success the plaintext is shown **once** (the
        Model.NewTokenPlaintext one-shot, the
        escalation.tokens.show_once warning, ESC·3) + a masked row in the
        list (the TokenPrefix only, ESC·3). The plaintext is **never**
        re-rendered on a subsequent GET (a fresh ListAsync projects to the
        EscalationTokenSummary — no plaintext, no TokenHash, ESC·3).
      - A **token list** (newest first, the IEscalationTokenService.ListAsync
        read — a read, no audit row, the M31·4 precedent). Each row: the
        Label + the masked TokenPrefix (the escalation.tokens.last_used label
        for the LastUsedAt? field, the U07 closed set) + the Created + the
        LastUsedAt? + a revoked chip (RevokedAt != null) + a Revoke button
        (the [ValidateAntiForgeryToken] POST to …/{id}/revoke, the
        IEscalationTokenService.RevokeAsync idempotent write lane, ESC·9).
      - An **empty state** (the escalation.tokens.none kw-l key, the U07
        closed set) when there are no tokens.

    The [Authorize(Roles = GlobalAdmin)] gate is the standard admin surface
    (the ErrorReportAdminController shape, the ADR 0001-B thin-token rule);
    no new AccessAction / Decide() branch / IAuthorizationService surface
    (ESC·12). The token validation stays in Core (the
    IEscalationTokenService.ValidateAsync seam, used by the inbound endpoint,
    U06) — this surface only generates / lists / revokes.

    The copy is the closed escalation.tokens.* kw-l key set (the U07 closed
    set, ESC·11 — the register's §2.3 keys 10–18). Every label goes through
    <kw-l> by key (the kw-l TagHelper floor, ADR 0015 D1 — an unregistered
    key falls back to the raw key, so the view renders the en reference text
    until U07 authors the values).

    Razor traps honored (AGENTS.md):
      - No <kw-l> inside a quoted attribute value (the chip uses a
        conditional @if/@else with separate <kw-l> elements).
      - No un-awaited Task<string> in markup (the flash strings are
        server-resolved by the controller's FlashAsync — the view only
        renders the resolved string).
      - No style=/data-* attributes built by interpolating quoted strings
        via @(...) (the Bootstrap classes are static strings).
      - The plaintext <code> block is a plain string (Model.NewTokenPlaintext
        is a server-resolved value, not a Task — the kw-l provider floor,
        ADR 0015 D1; the view renders it directly).
*@
@using Kumunita.Core.ErrorReports
@model Kumunita.Web.Models.EscalationTokenViewModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Admin — Receiving tokens";
}

@* The /admin section sub-nav (the ADR 0062 nav-tabs idiom): top of the page.
   This view sits in Views/Admin/Escalation/, so the shared partial — which
   lives in Views/Admin/ (the AdminController's own section) — must be
   referenced absolutely (the AdminStorage/Index.cshtml precedent). *@
@await Html.PartialAsync("~/Views/Admin/_AdminNav.cshtml")

<h1><kw-l key="escalation.tokens.title">Receiving access tokens</kw-l></h1>

@* The generate / revoke flash (the escalation.tokens.revoked key, the U07
   closed set, ESC·11) — rendered when the just-processed Revoke action was
   effective (a successful revocation). The Model.Flash is a server-resolved
   string (the controller's FlashAsync, the AdminOnboardingController.FlashAsync
   idiom). A no-op (an already-revoked token, ESC·9) sets no flash → no alert
   (the M32·8 idempotency precedent). *@
@if (Model.Flash is string flash)
{
    <div class="alert alert-success">@flash</div>
}

@* The validation error flash (a blank Label on Generate, the M32·4 / M31·6
   no-op shape). The Model.Error is a server-resolved string (the
   controller's FlashAsync, the kw-l provider floor, ADR 0015 D1). *@
@if (Model.Error is string err)
{
    <div class="alert alert-danger">@err</div>
}

@* The one-shot plaintext block (the ESC·3 pin — the plaintext is shown
   **exactly once**, the escalation.tokens.show_once warning). Rendered only
   when Model.NewTokenPlaintext is non-null (set on the re-render
   immediately after a Generate action, **never** on a subsequent GET — a
   fresh ListAsync projects to the EscalationTokenSummary read-model, which
   carries no plaintext and no TokenHash, ESC·3). A <code> block + a copy
   button (the escalation.tokens.copy kw-l key, the U07 closed set). *@
@if (Model.NewTokenPlaintext is string token)
{
    <div class="alert alert-warning">
        <p class="mb-2">
            <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.show_once">Copy this token now — it is shown only once and never stored in plain text.</kw-l>
        </p>
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <code class="flex-grow-1 break-all p-2 bg-white border rounded" id="new-token">@token</code>
            <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-primary text-nowrap"
                    onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(document.getElementById('new-token').textContent)">
                <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.copy">Copy</kw-l>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
}

@* The generate form (the escalation.tokens.generate.button + the
   escalation.tokens.label.label kw-l keys, the U07 closed set). A
   [ValidateAntiForgeryToken] POST to /admin/escalation/tokens/generate (the
   IEscalationTokenService.GenerateAsync single-write-lane, ESC·3 / ESC·9). *@
<form method="post" action="/admin/escalation/tokens/generate" class="card card-body mb-4">
    @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
    <div class="row g-2 align-items-end">
        <div class="col-md-8">
            <label class="form-label" for="label">
                <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.label.label">Label (e.g. the origin platform's name)</kw-l>
            </label>
            <input type="text" class="form-control" id="label" name="label" required />
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-4">
            <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary w-100">
                <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.generate.button">Generate a new token</kw-l>
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</form>

@* The token list (newest first, the IEscalationTokenService.ListAsync read,
   ESC·3 / ESC·9 — a read, no audit row, the M31·4 precedent). Each row: the
   Label + the masked TokenPrefix + the Created + the LastUsedAt? + a revoked
   chip (RevokedAt != null) + a Revoke button (the POST …/{id}/revoke, the
   IEscalationTokenService.RevokeAsync idempotent write lane, ESC·9). *@
@if (Model.Tokens.Count == 0)
{
    @* The empty state (the escalation.tokens.none kw-l key, the U07 closed
       set). *@
    <p class="text-muted">
        <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.none">No access tokens yet. Generate one to authorize an origin platform.</kw-l>
    </p>
}
else
{
    <div class="list-group kmb-escalation-tokens-list">
        @foreach (var t in Model.Tokens)
        {
            <div class="list-group-item d-flex align-items-start gap-3">
                @* The status chip: revoked = text-bg-danger (the
                   escalation.tokens.revoked kw-l key, the U07 closed set,
                   ESC·11 — the ESC·9 pin, the token no longer validates,
                   immediate). An active token shows a neutral success chip
                   (no dedicated "active" key in the §2.3 set — a static
                   Bootstrap badge, the M31 chip precedent). *@
                @if (t.RevokedAt is not null)
                {
                    <span class="badge text-bg-danger fw-semibold text-nowrap">
                        <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.revoked">Revoked</kw-l>
                    </span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span class="badge text-bg-success fw-semibold text-nowrap">
                        Active
                    </span>
                }
                <div class="flex-grow-1">
                    @* The label (the admin's name for the origin platform —
                       the ESC·3 pin, a plain string rendered as authored) +
                       the masked token prefix (the TokenPrefix is the masked
                       display form, e.g. "kesc_ab12…"; the plaintext + the
                       TokenHash are **never** exposed, the
                       EscalationTokenSummary read-model, ESC·3). *@
                    <div class="font-weight-semibold">
                        <span>@t.Label</span>
                        <code class="ms-2 fw-normal">@t.TokenPrefix</code>
                    </div>
                    @* The created timestamp (the kw-dt TagHelper — the house
                       date format, the ADR 0019/0020 surface). The
                       escalation.tokens.last_used kw-l key (the U07 closed
                       set) labels the last-used field below; the created
                       timestamp is a plain date (no dedicated "created" key
                       in the §2.3 set — the M31 list's created-date
                       precedent, the errorreport.list.created shape). *@
                    <div class="small mt-1 text-muted">
                        <kw-dt dt="@t.Created" format="g"></kw-dt>
                    </div>
                    @* The last-used timestamp (the kw-dt TagHelper, rendered
                       when non-null — the ESC·9 pin, the escalation.tokens.
                       last_used kw-l key, the U07 closed set). *@
                    @if (t.LastUsedAt is not null)
                    {
                        <div class="small mt-1">
                            <span class="text-muted">
                                <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.last_used">Last used</kw-l>
                            </span>
                            <kw-dt dt="@t.LastUsedAt.Value" format="g"></kw-dt>
                        </div>
                    }
                </div>
                @* The Revoke button (the [ValidateAntiForgeryToken] POST to
                   /admin/escalation/tokens/{id}/revoke, the
                   IEscalationTokenService.RevokeAsync idempotent write lane,
                   ESC·9). Visible only when the token is **not** already
                   revoked (a no-op — the M32·8 / M31·6 idempotency
                   precedent). *@
                @if (t.RevokedAt is null)
                {
                    <form method="post" action="/admin/escalation/tokens/@t.Id/revoke" class="ms-2 me-0">
                        @Html.AntiForgeryToken()
                        <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-danger text-nowrap">
                            <kw-l key="escalation.tokens.revoke.button">Revoke</kw-l>
                        </button>
                    </form>
                }
            </div>
        }
    </div>
}
